diff --git a/ARCHITECTURE.md b/ARCHITECTURE.md
index 9e3c0f1..7bc7e7d 100644
--- a/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@ Format: **recommendation**, alternatives, why, what would change my mind.
 - **Change my mind if:** you need a complex control (dialog, popover) that is costly to make accessible by hand.
 
 ### 3.8 Hosting
-- **Recommend:** Cloudflare Pages (or Workers static assets, see §0.6), free `.pages.dev` subdomain, build command `npx next build`, output directory `out` (from Cloudflare's static Next.js guide), connected to a GitHub repo for auto-deploy.
+- **Recommend:** Cloudflare Pages (or Workers static assets, see §0.6), free `.pages.dev` subdomain, build command `yarn build`, output directory `out` (from Cloudflare's static Next.js guide), connected to a GitHub repo for auto-deploy.
 - **Alternatives:** Vercel Hobby; GitHub Pages; Netlify.
 - **Why:** Free, global CDN, and the limits are not a concern for a small static site. Verified: Pages free limits are 500 builds/month, 20,000 files, 25 MiB per file, and Workers static assets are documented as free and unlimited.
 - **Commercial-use check (partly verified):** In Cloudflare's general terms and Self-Serve Subscription Agreement I found **no ban on commercial use of free plans**. Free Services are offered without liability and Cloudflare may end them at its sole discretion (§2.6), and you may not collect card details on a property receiving free services (§2.2.1(h)). Linking out to a Paystack page doesn't do that. I could **not** read the Developer Platform / service-specific terms, so that part is unconfirmed. For Vercel, I could not find the "non-commercial" wording on the Hobby and fair-use pages I fetched (parts rendered blank, and the terms page was blocked), so I can't confirm that claim from official text either. I've softened it in REQUIREMENTS.md.
diff --git a/BUILD_PLAN.md b/BUILD_PLAN.md
index ab0243d..ac1545b 100644
--- a/BUILD_PLAN.md
+++ b/BUILD_PLAN.md
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ Goal: a live `.pages.dev` URL showing the design tokens, so every later slice sh
   - Depends on: T1.1.
   - Done notes: first-load JS measured at 185.8 KB gzipped (test page, 20 icons); a bare page is 172.2 KB, so the framework floor alone is about 22 KB over the ~150 KB guess and the icons plus test block add about 13.6 KB. Decision: keep Next.js; the guess is unvalidated, Cloudflare will likely serve brotli (smaller than gzip), and the receipt renderer is already a lazy chunk. Judge by real phone load time after T1.3 and re-measure after Slice 3. Measured on Windows with a .NET gzip helper, so compare like with like. `scripts/check-icons.mjs` (`yarn check:icons`) is kept to re-verify icon names.
 - [ ] **T1.3 Deploy to Cloudflare** (0.5h)
-  - Build: connect the repo; build command `npx next build`, output directory `out` (from Cloudflare's static Next.js guide). Note whether the dashboard offers Pages or Workers static assets, and set a Node version if the build asks for one (check Cloudflare's build docs; not verified here). Add a stub `public/_headers` (no CSP yet).
+  - Build: connect the repo; build command `yarn build`, output directory `out` (from Cloudflare's static Next.js guide). Note whether the dashboard offers Pages or Workers static assets, and set a Node version if the build asks for one (check Cloudflare's build docs; not verified here). Add a stub `public/_headers` (no CSP yet).
   - Also: set the real `SITE_URL` in `config/index.ts` once the `.pages.dev` URL is known.
   - Done when: the `.pages.dev` URL loads on your phone over HTTPS; pushing to `main` redeploys.
   - Depends on: T1.1, T1.2.
